    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n74669" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀπτ-ικός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>of</i> or <i>for sight</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ ὀπτικά</span>”
				<i>the theory of the laws of sight, optics,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Metaph.</u>
					1077a5
				</span></i>
			, etc.; so <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ ὀπτική</span> (sc.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεωρία</span>) ib.<i><span class="en">
				997b20
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-καὶ ἀποδείξεις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>AP</u>
					0.76a24
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-κοὶ λόγοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Gal.
					17(2).214
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-κὴ δύναμις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					8.20
				</span></i>
			. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-κῶς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					18(1).309
				</span></i>
			.</div>
